column58:
I think this bit is particularly relevant,<p>> Any effort spent describing what methods to use on what URIs of interest should be entirely defined within the scope of the processing rules for a media type (and, in most cases, already defined by existing media types).<p>What are the "processing rules" for JSON? Do they depend on the application? Do we have a standard?<p>My first thought is something like this,<p><pre><code>    { "resources":
      { "foo":
        { href:   'http://example.com/foo',
          method: 'get'
        },
        "bar":
        { href:   'http://example.com/bar',
          method: 'post'
        },
        "baz":
        { href:   'http://example.com/baz',
          method: 'put'
        },
      }
    }</code></pre>
